#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:2
msgid "Parallel execution and HPC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:4
msgid ""
"PyHermes combines MPI ranks with Numba threads. The two levels serve "
"different purposes: MPI distributes independent fields, samples, or "
"modes; ``threads`` accelerates the numerical work local to each rank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:9
msgid "Launch pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:18
msgid ""
"Set the task's ``threads`` to the same value as the CPU allocation per "
"rank. Avoid nested oversubscription: ``ranks * threads`` should not "
"exceed the cores allocated by the scheduler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:23
msgid "How tasks distribute work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:25
msgid "Parallel work by task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:29
msgid "Task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:30
msgid "Main distribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:31
msgid "``SFCProjection``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:32
msgid ""
"Particles are divided across ranks and reduced into the shared MRA "
"coefficient field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:34
msgid "``Counting``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:35
msgid "Random evaluation positions are divided among ranks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:36
msgid "``Corr_2PCF``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:37
msgid "Separation samples and product work are distributed across ranks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:38
msgid "``Corr_3PCF``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:39
msgid "Centre and rotation work is distributed; rank 0 assembles outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:40
msgid "``Corr_3PCF_Multipole`` ``pair_mpi``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:41
msgid "Even rank pairs divide multipole-field convolution work for each sample."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:42
msgid "``Corr_3PCF_Multipole`` ``sample_mpi``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:43
msgid ""
"Radial samples are assigned round-robin, one rank per sample in the "
"current implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:47
msgid "Multipole CPU and GPU work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:49
msgid ""
"The 3PCF multipole convolution is CPU/MPI work for both backends. "
"``summation_backend`` changes the final filtered-field contraction only:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:59
msgid ""
"For ``sample_mpi`` on a CPU node, use approximately one rank per "
"concurrently active sample and assign several threads to each rank. On a "
"single-GPU node, many simultaneous GPU ranks usually contend for the same"
" device; ``pair_mpi`` or a smaller number of sample ranks is often easier"
" to tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:65
msgid "Memory planning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:67
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The base coefficient count is :math:`2^{3J}`. A one-level increase in "
"``J`` multiplies it by eight, and temporary real/complex FFT arrays "
"multiply the resident bytes further. MPI ranks may also hold rank-local "
"field buffers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:71
msgid "Practical rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:73
msgid "Validate a configuration at :math:`J=7` or :math:`J=8` before a large run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:74
msgid ""
"At high ``J``, prefer fewer ranks and more threads when rank-local field "
"replication dominates memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:76
msgid ""
"Use ``memory_strategy: memory`` for a many-product 2PCF when peak memory "
"is more important than rebuilding work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:78
msgid ""
"Enable field or kernel caches only when repeated computation outweighs "
"I/O; place caches on fast local storage when available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:80
msgid ""
"Request memory from measured ``MaxRSS`` plus headroom, not from the "
"serialized output size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:84
msgid "Input I/O"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:86
msgid ""
"In multipole ``sample_mpi`` mode, rank 0 reads a file-backed ``SFCField``"
" and broadcasts it. This reduces metadata and read contention on shared "
"storage. For large production arrays, storage location can still affect "
"startup and cache performance; copy hot inputs to node-local scratch if "
"the cluster makes that workflow available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:93
msgid "Slurm template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:110
msgid ""
"Scheduler syntax and MPI integration vary by site. If ``mpirun`` reports "
"that a rank spans CPU packages, adjust the scheduler's task placement or "
"mapper rather than enabling overload. A running process with poor binding"
" can be slower than a smaller, correctly placed job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:116
msgid "Measurement and reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:118
msgid ""
"Use the task logs for phase timings and Slurm accounting for whole-job "
"memory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../param/perform/perform.rst:125
msgid ""
"Keep ``base_seed`` or ``seed`` fixed when comparing algorithms. Repeat "
"timing runs under comparable node load; convolution-heavy workloads are "
"sensitive to memory bandwidth and CPU placement even when the estimator "
"output is identical."
msgstr ""
